{
  "id": "u09-l01",
  "unit": "u09-past",
  "title": "I did",
  "status": "draft",
  "tip": "The simple past for **আমি** (and **আমরা**) is verb stem + **-লাম** (*-lam*):\n\n- করা → **করলাম** 'I did'\n- দেখা → **দেখলাম** 'I saw / watched'\n- শোনা → **শুনলাম** 'I heard / listened'\n- পড়া → **পড়লাম** 'I read' (said *por-lam*)\n- বলা → **বললাম** 'I said / told' (said *bol-lam*)\n- ঘুমানো → **ঘুমালাম** 'I slept'\n- কেনা → **কিনলাম** 'I bought' (the vowel rises, as in কিনব)\n\nCompare the present you already know: **করি** 'I do' → **করলাম** 'I did'; **দেখি** 'I watch' → **দেখলাম** 'I watched'. The *-লাম* is the clue.\n\n**গতকাল** (*gotokal*) is 'yesterday'. Plain **কাল** means *either* yesterday or tomorrow; the verb tense tells you which. **আজ** is 'today'.\n\n**তাকে** (*take*) is 'him / her' as an object: **আমি তাকে বললাম** 'I told him/her'. Don't mix it up with **তার** 'his / her'.\n\n**Kolkata:** ঘুমালাম is often **ঘুমোলাম** (*ghumolam*).",
